      <bpmn:outgoing>chess-e10</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:userTask id="move" name="Plays a move">
      <bpmn:documentation>Everybody's, while it is Everybody's turn: anybody, a visitor filed under the device. Or a game of their own, the house's in either. A tap on a piece, then where it goes.
when: chess_move
ref: assets/chess.js press(), send()</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>chess-e6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>chess-e11</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:userTask id="undo" name="Takes it back, within ten seconds">
      <bpmn:documentation>Only in the tab that moved, and never a move that ended the game.
when: chess_undo
ref: assets/chess.js takeBack()</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>chess-e7</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>chess-e12</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="check" name="Checks it against the rules and files it">
      <bpmn:documentation>The move names the ply it answers, so somebody else's first is a 409 and the board redraws. The rules are held to published counts in CI.
ref: functions/api/chess.js POST move, undo
ref: functions/api/_chess.js
ref: tools/chessperf.mjs</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>chess-e11</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>chess-e12</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>chess-e13</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:userTask id="ask" name="Gives the game up, offers a draw, or agrees">
      <bpmn:documentation>Behind a confirm. One person resigns or offers alone; Everybody needs two names, a visitor counting. A player declines an offer; the city plays on instead.
when: chess_ask
when: chess_unask
when: chess_refuse
ref: assets/chess.js asksNode()</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>chess-e8</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>chess-e14</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="asked" name="Counts the names on the ask">
      <bpmn:documentation>Worked out from the rows and the moves on every read. An ask short of its names lapses two moves on.
ref: functions/api/chess.js POST ask, unask, refuse</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>chess-e14</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>chess-e15</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="over" name="Game over?">
      <bpmn:incoming>chess-e13</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>chess-e15</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>chess-e16</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>chess-e17</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="result" name="Records the result">
      <bpmn:documentation>Mate, stalemate, repetition, fifty moves, too little left, a resignation or a draw agreed. A public game given up or drawn starts the next one by itself.
ref: functions/api/chess.js finish(), endBy(), startPublic()</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>chess-e16</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>chess-e18</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="ended" name="The result on the board">
      <bpmn:incoming>chess-e18</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="updated" name="Every open page redraws on its next ask">
      <bpmn:incoming>chess-e17</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>chess-e20</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:userTask id="note" name="Leaves a note for whoever moves next">
      <bpmn:documentation>Under the public game while it is on. A member chooses whether their name goes on it; the author may delete it.
when: chess_note
when: chess_note_delete
ref: assets/chess.js noteComposer()</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>chess-e9</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>chess-e19</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="noted" name="Files the note, five an hour from one network">
      <bpmn:documentation>ref: functions/api/chess.js POST note, unnote</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>chess-e19</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>chess-e20</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="watch" name="Watches, with the radio on">
      <bpmn:incoming>chess-e10</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="m-what" name="What now?">
      <bpmn:incoming>chess-e4</bpmn:incoming>
